Lab: Create Azure Storage

Objective

Create an Azure Storage account. Then create a file share with on-premise files to synchronize with the cloud. 

Environment

Tools Used

Microsoft Azure Portal
Azure Resource Groups
Azure Subscription Management
Azure Storage Account

Operating System

Microsoft Azure

Skills Practiced

Cloud Administration
Resource Management
Azure Portal Navigation
Cloud Infrastructure Configuration
Cloud Storage Management

Actions Performed

1. Logged into MS Azure Portal.
2. On the Azure Home Page, the Resource Group and Storage Sync Service are listed under resources. 
3. Under the Azure Services is Storage accounts. I opened this page to configure the Storage account.  
4. The new page shows no previously created accounts. I clicked on Create.
5. In the Create a storage account page, I verified that the appropriate subscription and Resource group name were selected. 
6. In Instance Details, I provided a storage account name, provided the correct region, and selected the correct redundancy.
7. I reviewed the remaining options and reviewed my settings on the Review + create page to verify everything was correct before creating the account. Once verified, I created the storage account.
8. I opened the new storage account to create a file share between the Azure and on-site storage. This is located under Data Storage in the left side navigation pane. 
9. Once in the File share option, I clicked on File share and put the additional information into the settings. Once verified, all settings and information were correct, I created the File share. 
10. I verified the file share was active within the new Storage account. 
11. Documented findings and ended lab

Commands Used

None

Verification

After deploying the storage account, Azure sent me to a page showing the in-progress deployment of the account. Once complete, it displayed completion with the corresponding subscription and resource group. Also, going to the Azure Home Portal, I was able to see and confirm the status by clicking the Storage account hyperlink. After creating the file share, I verified it was active within the storage account. 

Issues Encountered

None

Resolution

Successfully deployed an Azure Storage Account within the selected subscription and region. Created and verified an Azure File share to support synchronization. confirmed all resources were available. 

Key Takeaways

Azure Storage Accounts provide scalable cloud-based storage services
Storage redundancy helps protect data availability and durability 

